--TEST--
`as` refuses every operand/target pair `rule:types/conversion`'s table has no row for, one diagnostic per pair — `rule:types/conversion`, `rule:types/conversion`, `rule:types/conversion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/conversion`'s table is *closed*: `as` "either produces a value of the
// target type or throws", so a pair naming no row has nothing to produce and
// nothing to throw. Each binding below is one absent row, and each help names
// the spelling that says what was meant instead.
enum Mode { Read, Write }

class Helper {
    public static function nothing(): void {}
}

class Foo { public int $n = 1; }
class Bar { public string $m = "x"; }

array<int> $xs = [1, 2];
bool $flag = true;
int $i = 7;
string $s = "abc";
Mode $mode = Mode::Read;
Foo $foo = new Foo();

// An `array<T>` and an enum case have no text of their own: the "anything →
// `string`" row is total for *scalars*, and neither is one.
string $a = $xs as string;
string $b = $mode as string;
// `rule:types/conversion` grants an enum its own backing type and no other number.
float $c = $mode as float;
// `bool` is in the `string` row and in no numeric one.
int $d = $flag as int;
// `rule:types/conversion` gives `bytes` exactly one source and one target, both `string`.
bytes $e = $i as bytes;
// The only row producing an `array<T>` is another `array<U>`.
array<int> $f = $s as array<int>;
// No row produces a class. `Foo` and `Bar` share one representation, so this
// is the pair that would otherwise read `Bar`'s slot list off a `Foo`.
Bar $g = $foo as Bar;
// A `void` call has no value at all, so it is neither an operand nor a target.
string $h = Helper::nothing() as string;
// `as` never substitutes a default, which is the whole of what this would be.
int $j = null as int;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0708]: `array<int>` cannot be converted to `string`
%A
error[E0708]: `Mode` cannot be converted to `string`
%A
error[E0708]: `Mode` cannot be converted to `float`
%A
error[E0708]: `bool` cannot be converted to `int`
%A
error[E0708]: `int` cannot be converted to `bytes`
%A
error[E0708]: `string` cannot be converted to `array<int>`
%A
error[E0708]: `Foo` cannot be converted to `Bar`
%A
error[E0708]: `void` cannot be converted to `string`
%A
error[E0708]: `null` cannot be converted to `int`
%A
